  "complexity": 6,
  "title": "fix round 1 (review): landing: S2d1 cache-aware context router in shadow: cacheability, effective cache cost and",
  "spec": "Fix round 1 for T-1282: review T-1288 requested changes. fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/context_router.py:123 [high]: The new fallback branch returns the reason test_result for items that used to get ambiguous. That changes the ambiguous list, the ambiguous counts and the reduction stats in shadow mode, and it breaks the rule that shadow must not change existing routing output. fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/context_router.py:11 [high]: FALLBACK_REASONS holds invented strings, not the reason strings _choice already assigns when no named rule matched. Downgrade eligibility therefore does not follow the spec and the docs' verbatim list. The set contains a source_type worker_partial that the code never treats as a fallback reason. fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/spawn.py:1122 [med]: scout_packet now routes a synthetic candidate through _shadow_route, writing decision_log rows and passing routing metadata into _role_packet. The task did not ask for this, and it changes how scout packets are recorded. fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/spawn.py:396 [low]: _context_mode stores the flag _context_cache_invalid in the shared cfg dict. Route() then re-validates cache_mode itself, so the validation happens twice and cfg carries hidden state. Pass the flag through explicitly instead. fix round 1 rule: Restore the original _choice behaviour for items that used to get the reason ambiguous (no new test_result fallback branch; the ambiguous list, counts and reduction stats in shadow are byte-identical to before this task, add a test). FALLBACK_REASONS must contain exactly the reason strings _choice assigns when no named rule matched, taken from the code, not invented names, and no source_type names; the docs list them verbatim. Revert the scout_packet change: scout packets must not route a synthetic candidate through _shadow_route or write decision_log rows. Remove the hidden _context_cache_invalid flag from cfg: _context_mode returns the effective mode and the invalid flag explicitly and route() receives cache_mode as an argument, validated once. Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until it exits 0; do not ask questions; report files changed and failures-only output.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_context_router.py::test_cache_fields_on_rows_and_presented_level_unchanged_in_shadow (route() levels identical with cache_mode shadow and with no cache_mode key; deterministic maps present)",
    "tests/test_context_router.py::test_cache_adjusted_level_algorithm (downgrade only for eligible dynamic items; named-rule reasons untouched; HIDE untouched; provider None gives cache_cost None)",
    "tests/test_context_router.py::test_active_cache_mode_applies_adjusted_levels_only_when_mode_not_off",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_scorecard_context_cache_shadow_summary",
    "tests/test_context_router.py::test_cache_mode_helper_validates_and_shadow_keeps_candidates_byte_identical",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_route_receives_effective_mode_and_provider",
    "tests/test_context_router.py::test_invalid_cache_mode_falls_back_to_off_with_flag",
    "the worktree log between goal/T-0991 and HEAD contains the cherry-picked change and HEAD descends from the goal head",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0",
    "fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/context_router.py:123 [high]: The new fallback branch returns the reason test_result for items that used to get ambiguous. That changes the ambiguous list, the ambiguous counts and the reduction stats in shadow mode, and it breaks the rule that shadow must not change existing routing output.",
    "fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/context_router.py:11 [high]: FALLBACK_REASONS holds invented strings, not the reason strings _choice already assigns when no named rule matched. Downgrade eligibility therefore does not follow the spec and the docs' verbatim list. The set contains a source_type worker_partial that the code never treats as a fallback reason.",
    "fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/spawn.py:1122 [med]: scout_packet now routes a synthetic candidate through _shadow_route, writing decision_log rows and passing routing metadata into _role_packet. The task did not ask for this, and it changes how scout packets are recorded.",
    "fix round 1: address review T-1288 comment orchestrator/spawn.py:396 [low]: _context_mode stores the flag _context_cache_invalid in the shared cfg dict. Route() then re-validates cache_mode itself, so the validation happens twice and cfg carries hidden state. Pass the flag through explicitly instead.",
    "fix round 1 rule: Restore the original _choice behaviour for items that used to get the reason ambiguous (no new test_result fallback branch; the ambiguous list, counts and reduction stats in shadow are byte-identical to before this task, add a test). FALLBACK_REASONS must contain exactly the reason strings _choice assigns when no named rule matched, taken from the code, not invented names, and no source_type names; the docs list them verbatim. Revert the scout_packet change: scout packets must not route a synthetic candidate through _shadow_route or write decision_log rows. Remove the hidden _context_cache_invalid flag from cfg: _context_mode returns the effective mode and the invalid flag explicitly and route() receives cache_mode as an argument, validated once."
  ],
